msgid ""
"Your policy captures 71％ of the grid import a perfectly-informed battery "
"could have avoided. Allowed to export, that ceiling rises to 2,311 kWh (a"
" 61％ capture) — the extra is arbitrage your export setting currently "
"forbids."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your prices change every 15 minutes but your meter records hourly, so the"
" run sees one averaged price per hour and cannot act on within-hour "
"swings."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your smart meter only sees energy crossing the grid connection, so "
"household consumption is reconstructed: load = grid import − grid export "
"+ solar produced + battery discharged − battery charged. Because you have"
" an existing battery, its charge and discharge are included, so this is "
"your consumption net of that battery. Intervals where the result is "
"negative (a data problem) are clamped to zero."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your smart meter only sees energy crossing the grid connection, so "
"household consumption is reconstructed: load = grid import − grid export "
"+ solar produced. Intervals where the result is negative (a data problem)"
" are clamped to zero."
